Strategy for Naive player -
    Places its mark in the first available cell.
Strategy for Smart player -
    Plays a turn by first blocking the NaivePlayer's move at (0,1),
    then placing its mark in the first available cell on the board.
Strategy for Whatever player -
    Puts a mark in a random position on the board.

The advantage of designing the program so that each player class implements a shared interface
is that it allows the Game and Tournament to treat all player types
in the same way, regardless of their internal logic.
It's based on polymorphism, abstraction, and encapsulation.